## Usage

`TxVoiceRing` draws a voice-reactive spectrum ribbon (`ring`) or twin grey tubes (`mono`) that bend with speech energy, shift colour with emotion, and lean toward a speaker direction. Drive it with a microphone `MediaStream`, a Web Audio `AnalyserNode`, or a per-frame `level` getter.

### Ring variants, states, and emotion tint

Switch between luminous `ring` and sculptural `mono`, cycle through all four conversation states, try emotion hues, or switch to live microphone capture.

:::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="VoiceRingBasicDemo" code-lang="vue"}
---
code: |
  <script setup lang="ts">
  import { TxVoiceRing, useVoiceRingMicrophone } from '@talex-touch/tuffex/voice-ring'

  const mic = useVoiceRingMicrophone()
  </script>

  <template>
    <TxVoiceRing
      type="ring"
      state="listening"
      :size="220"
      :stream="mic.stream.value"
      emotion="calm"
      hover-bend
    />
  </template>
---
:::

### Spatial speaker lean and edge refraction

Pass `direction` (`-1` left to `+1` right) to lean, stretch, and refract the ring against `directionBounds`. Move the pointer across the stage below to drive live directional tracking and telemetry.

:::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="VoiceRingSpatialDemo" code-lang="vue"}
---
code: |
  <script setup lang="ts">
  import { ref } from 'vue'
  import { TxVoiceRing } from '@talex-touch/tuffex/voice-ring'

  const pan = ref(-0.7)
  const containerRef = ref<HTMLElement | null>(null)
  </script>

  <template>
    <div ref="containerRef" style="overflow: hidden">
      <TxVoiceRing
        state="listening"
        :size="180"
        :level="0.65"
        :direction="pan"
        :direction-bounds="containerRef"
      />
    </div>
  </template>
---
:::

### Best Practices

- Pass a getter function to `level` (`() => currentLevel`) instead of mutating a reactive prop 60 times a second.
- When enabling `direction` inside a card or sheet, pass the host element to `directionBounds` with `overflow: hidden` so the edge glass lens meets the container cleanly.
- Browser microphones are typically mono; supply `direction` from stereo capture, speaker diarisation, or spatial UI layout.
- Provide localized state text via `labels` for screen readers.

## API Reference

### Props

| Name | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `type` | `'ring' \| 'mono'` | `'ring'` | Luminous chromatic spectrum `ring` or twin-tube `mono`. |
| `state` | `'idle' \| 'listening' \| 'speaking' \| 'processing'` | `'listening'` | Conversation state; `idle` and `processing` ignore external audio input. |
| `size` | `number` | `160` | Logical ring diameter in CSS pixels. |
| `stream` | `MediaStream \| null` | `null` | Live audio stream (wins over `analyser` and `level`). |
| `analyser` | `AnalyserNode \| null` | `null` | Existing Web Audio `AnalyserNode` (wins over `level`). |
| `level` | `number \| (() => number)` | — | Manual voice level (`0–1`) or per-frame getter. |
| `emotion` | `'positive' \| 'negative' \| 'calm' \| null` | `null` | Emotion colour shift with smooth crossfade transitions. |
| `direction` | `number \| (() => number)` | — | Speaker pan (`-1` left … `+1` right) or per-frame getter. |
| `directionBounds` | `Element \| Ref<Element \| null> \| null` | Viewport | Bounding element or template ref clamping horizontal lean. |
| `directionMove` | `number` | Preset default | Horizontal drift factor when leaning toward a speaker. |
| `directionLens` | `number` | Preset default | Edge glass refraction intensity against bounds (`0–2`). |
| `hoverBend` | `boolean \| number` | `false` | Membrane pull toward a hovering fine pointer while idle or processing. |
| `theme` | `'auto' \| 'dark' \| 'light'` | `'auto'` | Substrate theme; `auto` follows ancestor `.dark` / `data-theme` and OS scheme. |
| `sensitivity` | `number` | `0.85` | Input audio gain multiplier. |
| `threshold` | `number` | `0.04` | Noise gate floor below which input reads as silence. |
| `speed` | `number` | `1` | Internal animation clock speed multiplier. |
| `paused` | `boolean` | `false` | Freezes on the current frame and halts the frame loop. |
| `ariaLabel` | `string` | `labels[state]` | Explicit accessible label for the canvas. |
| `labels` | `Partial<VoiceRingLabels>` | English defaults | State labels exposed to assistive technology. |

### Events

| Event | Payload | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `level` | `value: number` | Fired per frame with the smoothed voice level (`0–1`). |

### Composables

| Composable | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `useVoiceRingMicrophone(options?)` | Manages microphone permission, raw audio stream acquisition, and unmount track cleanup. |

## Overview

- Combined `IntersectionObserver` and `visibilitychange` gates pause the frame loop automatically when offscreen or hidden.
- With `direction` enabled, the canvas widens symmetrically with matching negative margins so leaning glow never clips or shifts layout.
- Respects `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`, holding a static frame without an active audio source.

## Technologies

- Geometry, edge refraction lens (2D Canvas + lightweight WebGL edge pass), and voice envelope follower ported from [Jakubantalik/Libraries.dev · voice-ring](https://github.com/Jakubantalik/Libraries.dev/tree/main/packages/voice-ring) (MIT © 2026 Jakub Antalik).
- Source path: `packages/tuffex/packages/components/src/voice-ring/`.

